#X obj 667 11 seq.markov;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 200 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object generates melodies using a Markov chain.
It learns note transitions from the incoming note messages and then
generates new sequences based on the learned probabilities;
#X text 240 153 @order sets the order of the Markov chain: 0 — order
0 (random notes) \, 1 — order 1 (each note depends on the previous
one) \, 2 — order 2 (each note depends on the two previous ones);
#X text 240 223 the first outlet outputs the generated MIDI pitch \,
the second outlet outputs the duration bin;
